---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Draw a board or a part of it as a PNG or SVG picture.
The file goes to ~/Downloads unless a file is given; it only reads the board.

USAGE
  holst board snap <board> [<file>] [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board to draw
  file    A new .png or .svg file, never overwritten, - for stdout; ~/Downloads/<name>-<id>.png by default

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws        Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --rectangle x,y,w,h   An area as a rectangle: x,y,width,height in board units
      --frame frame         An area as a frame: id, link, title or part of a title
      --object object       An object, repeat for several: id, link, @N or the first 8 characters of its id
      --padding units       Padding around a frame or objects in board units; 16 and 40 by default
      --refresh             Ignore the cached copy and download the board again
      --offline             No network: use the cached copy, or fail when there is none
      --format format       The picture format: png or svg; from the file's extension, else png
      --scale scale         Pixels per board unit, lowered so the picture fits --max-side; 1 by default
      --max-side px         The longest side in pixels; 8192 by default
      --embed               Put the images into an SVG instead of links to the storage

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst b snap "Roadmap"
  $ holst b snap "Roadmap" --frame "Q3" q3.png
  $ holst b snap "Roadmap" --object a1b2c3d4 --embed q3.svg

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
